One goroutine per input copying into a shared `out`, a `sync.WaitGroup` counting them, and a closer goroutine:

```go
func merge(cs ...<-chan int) <-chan int {
  out := make(chan int); var wg sync.WaitGroup
  for _, c := range cs { wg.Add(1); go func(c <-chan int){ defer wg.Done(); for v := range c { out <- v } }(c) }
  go func(){ wg.Wait(); close(out) }()
  return out
}
```

The `wg.Wait(); close(out)` in its own goroutine is the crux — close once, after every input finishes.
